rmv0" spacing=3D"loose"><h2 id=3D"heading-intro" class=3D"g-md-h2">Intro</h=
2>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">One of the benefits of <a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"htt=
ps://www.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/article/how-to-use-jupyter-notebooks" class=3D"g-md=
-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0">working in Jupyter Notebook</a> is t=
hat you can have much more functionality and expression than when working d=
irectly in your terminal. This includes adding markdown to customize and st=
yle text outside of code blocks, adding mathematical equations with LaTeX, =
using hotkeys for shortcuts, and lastly using magic commands that come with=
 IPython that yield greater efficiency for  common tasks.</p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">If you haven=E2=80=99t already, <a target=3D"_blank" hr=
ef=3D"https://www.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/article/setting-up-jupyter-notebook" class=
=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0">install Jupyter Notebook</a>=
 on your computer before reading the rest of the article.</p>
<h2 id=3D"heading-markdown-in-jupyter-notebook" class=3D"g-md-h2">Markdown =
in Jupyter Notebook</h2>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://www.markdownguide.=
org/" class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0" rel=3D"noopener">=
Markdown</a> was created in 2004 to allow users to create rich text using p=
lain text which is easy to read and write. What is rich text vs plain text?=
 The difference is that rich text is a file format that allows for formatti=
ng and styling whereas plain text contains no formatting, being made up sol=
ely of text, line breaks, and spacing. </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Markdown is a great technology because you can type pla=
in text and it will get rendered into styled text without having to click a=
ny icons, and it=E2=80=99ll be done programmatically. We=E2=80=99ll dive in=
to the markdown syntax that you can add to markdown chunks in your notebook=
.</p>
<h3 id=3D"heading-markdown-cells" class=3D"g-md-h3">Markdown Cells</h3>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">When you create a new cell, you have a few options in t=
he drop down menu. When working with Markdown, make sure your cell is of th=
e Markdown type, and not of the others.</p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"Image of the Jupyter notebook cell types ac=
cessed from the dropdown menu." class=3D"g-md-img" src=3D"https://content.c=
odecademy.com/programs/data-science-path/juptyer_notebook_setup/multiple_ce=
lls.png"></p>
<h3 id=3D"heading-headings" class=3D"g-md-h3">Headings</h3>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">There are six levels of headings available. These are u=
seful for organizing sections in your code. You use the octothorp, also cal=
led hashtag <code class=3D"g-md-code">#</code> and add the number of them t=
hat correspond to the heading level. </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"Image demonstrating code for the six headin=
g sizes in a markdown cell and an example of the resulting output." class=
=3D"g-md-img" src=3D"https://content.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/programs/data-science-p=
ath/juptyer_notebook_setup/headings.png"></p>
<h3 id=3D"heading-styling" class=3D"g-md-h3">Styling</h3>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">You can add some styling with Strong and Emphasized tex=
t. In HTML there  are the <code class=3D"g-md-code">&lt;strong&gt; </code> =
and <code class=3D"g-md-code">&lt;em&gt;</code> tags that denote different =
messages. Strong text shows strong importance for its contents,  while emph=
asis is used to change the tone of a word or phrase as it might be emphasiz=
ed in speech. Example (=E2=80=9CI <em class=3D"g-md-em">hate</em> cilantro=
=E2=80=9D vs. =E2=80=9CI hate cilantro=E2=80=9D).</p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">You can get emphasized text with either one asterisk <c=
ode class=3D"g-md-code">*</code> or underscore <code class=3D"g-md-code">_<=
/code> around the text. For Strong styling use two  asterisks <code class=
=3D"g-md-code">**</code> or underscores <code class=3D"g-md-code">__</code>=
 around the text.</p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"Image demonstrating code for the Strong and=
 Emphasized text styling in a markdown cell and an example of the resulting=
 output." class=3D"g-md-img" src=3D"https://content.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/programs=
/data-science-path/juptyer_notebook_setup/strong.png"></p>
<h3 id=3D"heading-code-monospace" class=3D"g-md-h3">Code (monospace)</h3>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">If you want to make monospace text which is good for de=
noting code, use a single <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">`</strong> called a=
 back tick, back quote, or left quote around the text. </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"Image demonstrating code for a monospace in=
 a markdown cell and an example of the resulting output." class=3D"g-md-img=
" src=3D"https://content.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/programs/data-science-path/juptyer_=
notebook_setup/monospace.png"></p>
<h3 id=3D"heading-line-breaks" class=3D"g-md-h3">Line Breaks</h3>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">You can create new lines either by including a new line=
 in the code, or using <code class=3D"g-md-code">&lt;br&gt;</code> inline w=
ith text. Using <code class=3D"g-md-code">***</code> will give you a horizo=
ntal line. </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"Image demonstrating code for a line break i=
n a markdown cell and an example of the resulting output." class=3D"g-md-im=
g" src=3D"https://content.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/programs/data-science-path/juptyer=
_notebook_setup/line_break.png"></p>
<h3 id=3D"heading-lists-unordered-and-ordered" class=3D"g-md-h3">Lists (Uno=
rdered and Ordered)</h3>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">For unordered lists use a hyphen <code class=3D"g-md-co=
de">-</code> or asterisk <code class=3D"g-md-code">*</code> with a space be=
fore the text. If you want a sub bullet add a tab before the hyphen <code c=
lass=3D"g-md-code">-</code> or asterisk <code class=3D"g-md-code">*</code>.=
 </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"Image demonstrating code for an unordered l=
ist in a markdown cell and an example of the resulting output." class=3D"g-=
md-img" src=3D"https://content.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/programs/data-science-path/ju=
ptyer_notebook_setup/unordered_list.png"></p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">For ordered lists, use numbers followed by a period for=
 the items like so <code class=3D"g-md-code">1.</code>. Tabs still work for=
 sub ordered lists. </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"Image demonstrating code for an ordered lis=
t in a markdown cell and an example of the resulting output." class=3D"g-md=
-img" src=3D"https://content.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/programs/data-science-path/jupt=
yer_notebook_setup/ordered_list.png"></p>
<h3 id=3D"heading-images" class=3D"g-md-h3">Images</h3>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">You can add images from your directory or from the web =
<code class=3D"g-md-code">![title](img/picture.png)</code>. In between the =
two brackets our image name will take the place of title, and within the pa=
rentheses, the file path or url will take the place of img/picture.png.</p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"Image demonstrating code for adding an imag=
e in a markdown cell and an example of the resulting output of the codecade=
my logo." class=3D"g-md-img" src=3D"https://content.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/programs=
/data-science-path/juptyer_notebook_setup/image_example.png"></p>
<h3 id=3D"heading-links-external-and-internal" class=3D"g-md-h3">Links (Ext=
ernal and Internal)</h3>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Adding external links are just like images without the =
exclamation point. Here is how you do it <code class=3D"g-md-code">[link te=
xt](http://url)</code>:</p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"Image demonstrating code for an external li=
nk in a markdown cell and an example of the resulting output." class=3D"g-m=
d-img" src=3D"https://content.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/programs/data-science-path/jup=
tyer_notebook_setup/links.png"></p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Adding internal sections are even easier just use <code=
 class=3D"g-md-code">[section title](#section-title)</code>:</p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"Image demonstrating code for an external li=
nk in a markdown cell and an example of the resulting output." class=3D"g-m=
d-img" src=3D"https://content.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/programs/data-science-path/jup=
tyer_notebook_setup/sections.png"></p>
<h4 id=3D"heading-hotkeys-in-jupyter-notebook" class=3D"g-md-h4">Hotkeys in=
 Jupyter Notebook</h4>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Hotkeys or keyboard shortcuts can improve your efficien=
cy and save time when you=E2=80=99re working with a new program. Instead of=
 using your mouse which takes your hands off of the keyboard, you can acces=
s many of the common functionality with a combination of keys. Jupyter Note=
book keyboard shortcuts can be accessed through <code class=3D"g-md-code">h=
elp&gt;keyboard shortcuts</code>. You can also access them through pressing=
 the <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">Cmd</strong> + <strong class=3D"g-md-str=
ong">Shift</strong> + <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">P</strong> keys for Mac=
 or <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">Ctrl</strong> + <strong class=3D"g-md-str=
ong">Shift</strong> + <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">P</strong> for Linux/Wi=
ndows to open the command palette. Through the palette you can search for k=
eywords and find the command or use commands that don=E2=80=99t have a keyb=
oard shortcut. </p>
<h5 id=3D"heading-basic-commands" class=3D"g-md-h5">Basic Commands</h5>
<ul class=3D"g-md-ul">
<li class=3D"g-md-li">Basic navigation: <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">Enter=
</strong>, <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">Shift</strong>-<strong class=3D"g-=
md-strong">Enter</strong>, <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">Up</strong>/<stron=
g class=3D"g-md-strong">k</strong>, <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">Down</str=
ong>/<strong class=3D"g-md-strong">j</strong>.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">Saving the notebook: <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">s<=
/strong>.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">Change Cell types: <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">m</s=
trong> to change the current cell to Markdown, <strong class=3D"g-md-strong=
">y</strong> to change it back to code.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">Cell creation: <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">a</stron=
g> to insert a new cell above the current cell, <strong class=3D"g-md-stron=
g">b</strong> to insert a new cell below.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">Cell editing: <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">x</strong=
>, <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">c</strong>, <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">=
v</strong>, <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">d</strong>, <strong class=3D"g-md=
-strong">z</strong> </li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">Delete Current Cell: <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">d<=
/strong> + <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">d</strong> (press the key twice).<=
/li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">Kernel operations: <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">i</s=
trong>, <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">0</strong> (press twice).</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">Split the current cell into two: <strong class=3D"g-m=
d-strong">Ctrl</strong> + <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">Shift</strong> + <s=
trong class=3D"g-md-strong">-</strong>. </li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">Find and replace on your code: <strong class=3D"g-md-=
strong">Esc</strong> + <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">f</strong></li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">Toggle cell output: <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">Esc=
</strong> + <strong class=3D"g-md-strong">O</strong></li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"heading-latex-in-jupyter-notebook" class=3D"g-md-h2">LaTeX in Jup=
yter Notebook</h2>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://www.latex-project.=
org/" class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0" rel=3D"noopener">=
LaTeX</a> is useful for mathematical and scientific writing. For example, s=
howing equations through plain text is difficult and not easily readable. L=
aTeX allows users to create math equations like you see in textbooks or whe=
n you write them on a chalkboard. </p>
<h4 id=3D"heading-inputting-latex" class=3D"g-md-h4">Inputting LaTeX</h4>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">In the markdown cell, you can add LaTeX code between <c=
ode class=3D"g-md-code">$</code> for inline outputs. You can also use two <=
code class=3D"g-md-code">$$</code> to create its own centered paragraph in =
display mode.</p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"Image demonstrating code for the Classifica=
tion Rate formual described in LaTeX in a markdown cell and an example of t=
he resulting output." class=3D"g-md-img" src=3D"https://content.AI Academy by RiWoT.=
com/programs/data-science-path/juptyer_notebook_setup/latex.png"></p>
<h5 id=3D"heading-important-notes" class=3D"g-md-h5">Important Notes:</h5>
<ul class=3D"g-md-ul">
<li class=3D"g-md-li">To add a little spacing in display mode, use <code cl=
ass=3D"g-md-code">\</code></li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">To add a new line when in math display mode, use <cod=
e class=3D"g-md-code">\\</code></li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">To display a fraction, use <code class=3D"g-md-code">=
\frac{arg 1}{arg 2}</code></li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">For power (superscripts text), use <code class=3D"g-m=
d-code">^{}</code></li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">For indices (subscripts), use <code class=3D"g-md-cod=
e">_{}</code></li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">For roots, use <code class=3D"g-md-code">\sqrt[n]{arg=
}</code></li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">The <code class=3D"g-md-code">[n]</code> is optional.=
</li>
</ul>
<h4 id=3D"heading-greek-letters" class=3D"g-md-h4">Greek Letters</h4>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Add <code class=3D"g-md-code">\</code> to create Greek =
letters. Capitalization also works.</p>
<h4 id=3D"heading-mathematical-symbols" class=3D"g-md-h4">Mathematical Symb=
ols</h4>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"Image demonstrating the various mathematica=
l symbols that can be called in Jupyter notebook." class=3D"g-md-img" src=
=3D"https://content.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/programs/data-science-path/juptyer_noteb=
ook_setup/math.png"></p>
<h4 id=3D"heading-magic-commands-in-jupyter-notebook" class=3D"g-md-h4">Mag=
ic Commands in Jupyter Notebook</h4>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">There are also magic commands that can be used when con=
ducting data analysis in Ipython. Magic commands  will help you complete co=
mmonly executed tasks in your notebook, and come in two varieties; line mag=
ics and cell magics. Line magics contain a single percent symbol <code clas=
s=3D"g-md-code">%</code> prefix and work on a single line of input. Cell ma=
gics contain a double percent sign <code class=3D"g-md-code">%%</code> pref=
ix and work on multiple lines of input. Here are some examples of magic com=
mands:</p>
<ul class=3D"g-md-ul">
<li class=3D"g-md-li"><code class=3D"g-md-code">%lsmagic</code>: Return a l=
ist of all magic commands</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li"><code class=3D"g-md-code">%run</code>: Execute extern=
al python script</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li"><code class=3D"g-md-code">%load</code>: Load in a loc=
al file, URL, function, or class</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li"><code class=3D"g-md-code">%who</code>: Return a list =
of any variables that have a certain type within the notebook.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li"><code class=3D"g-md-code">%matplotlib notebook</code>=
: Allow you to interactively work with plots from <code class=3D"g-md-code"=
>matplotlib</code>. </li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li"><code class=3D"g-md-code">%matplotlib inline</code>: =
Allow you to disable interactivity with plots.</li>
<li class=3D"g-md-li"><code class=3D"g-md-code">%%time</code>: Show the tim=
e it took to execute the line of code. Good for checking efficiency.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"heading-other-tips" class=3D"g-md-h2">Other Tips</h2>
<h4 id=3D"heading-pretty-displays" class=3D"g-md-h4">Pretty Displays</h4>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Displays all variables and statements on its own line</=
p>
<pre class=3D"g-md-pre"><pre class=3D"gamut-mu6hz5 e1rzuoz70"><code><div da=
ta-lang=3D"AI Academy by RiWoT-python" class=3D"gamut-1rlug0v epnovk10"><span><span =
class=3D"mtk12">from</span><span class=3D"mtk1"> </span><span class=3D"mtk9=
">IPython</span><span class=3D"mtk1">.</span><span class=3D"mtk10">core</sp=
an><span class=3D"mtk9">.</span><span class=3D"mtk10">interactiveshell</spa=
n><span class=3D"mtk1"> </span><span class=3D"mtk12">import</span><span cla=
ss=3D"mtk1"> </span><span class=3D"mtk9">InteractiveShell</span></span><br>=
<span><span class=3D"mtk9">InteractiveShell</span><span class=3D"mtk1">.</s=
pan><span class=3D"mtk10">ast_node_interactivity</span><span class=3D"mtk1"=
